# hud-quads.xrs - the HUD's anchors reach the compositor (VR-117, VR-120).
#
# The runtime submits the HUD as quad layers, so it exists only in the
# compositor: quadLayers is the field that sees it, and the per-shot JSON
# carries each layer's space and pose. Run this in GAMEPLAY (walk in first)
# with stereo reentry armed, or the gate is down by design and nothing arms.
# The sim's left hand is posed where a controller would be held, so the hand
# anchor has something to locate. `hud anchor all <anchor>` moves EVERY row
# (VR-120), so the whole HUD follows one anchor as it did with one element.
#
#   tools\xrsim-run.ps1 -Path tools\xrsim\hud-quads.xrs -Dir D:\dvr-data\xrsim
reset
hand l grip pose -0.20 1.10 -0.40 0 0 0
# The aim dot (VR-57) is a quad layer too: park it so quadLayers counts the HUD alone.
@mod stereo reentry; crosshair dot off
@frames 240
@assert sessionState eq FOCUSED
@assert projectionViews eq 2

# The whole HUD on the window (the preset): every quad in VIEW space.
@mod hud on; hud anchor all window
@frames 180
@assert projectionViews eq 2
@assert quadLayers ge 1
@shot hud_window
@assert capNonBlackL ge 30
@assert capNonBlackR ge 30

# The whole HUD on the LEFT HAND: LOCAL space, at the posed grip.
@mod hud anchor all handL
@frames 120
@assert quadLayers ge 1
@shot hud_hand

# An untracked hand submits NO quad rather than a stale one.
hand l valid off
@frames 120
@assert quadLayers eq 0
@shot hud_hand_untracked
hand l valid on
@frames 120
@assert quadLayers ge 1

# The world-locked window stays put when the head turns (compare the pose in
# hud_world_a.json with hud_world_b.json: same LOCAL position).
@mod hud anchor all world; hud window recenter
@frames 120
@assert quadLayers ge 1
@shot hud_world_a
head rot 0 30 0
@frames 120
@shot hud_world_b
head rot 0 0 0

# And back to the preset, with the aim dot back.
@mod hud anchor all window; crosshair dot on
@frames 60
@assert quadLayers ge 2
